  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support Strategic Dialogue Lowland Development and Irrigation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implemented from November 2023 to July 2024, the project aimed to advance strategic dialogue under the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Water, focusing on lowland development and irrigation &#x2013; key aspects of sustainable water and agricultural resource management. It facilitated a joint process between Indonesian and Dutch representatives to develop a preliminary vision on potential areas of collaboration and to propose a concrete scope of work for a future multi-year strategic programme. This included defining interim milestones to guide continued dialogue from the Joint Steering Committee (JSC) session forward.Activities were guided by a joint core team from both governments and involved one-on-one consultations and multi-stakeholder dialogues to ensure inclusive input into the strategic outlook. Results informed a reconnaissance of opportunities for cooperation, clarified collaboration opportunities in agricultural water resources and irrigation governance, and outlined practical steps for sustained engagement.The project contributed to strengthening policy dialogue and cooperation foundations for integrated lowland development and irrigation initiatives within the broader Indonesia-Netherlands bilateral water partnership.</narrative>
  </description>
